# Radar for WebCLAP

Radar, a loop player: a ray turns once per loop, reflects off segments drawn into a circle, and where it leaves the
circle picks the position in the sample. A rewrite for WebCLAP of radar's TypeScript, presented at Flash on the
Beach in 2009, with an editor of its own, twelve patterns and a device panel for openDAW.

- radar: https://github.com/andremichelle/radar
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-radar.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

